ponents, and manages third-party CSS.",[225,1396,1397,1399,1400,1402,1403,1406,1407,1409,1410,250,1412,240],{},[1372,1398,1374],{},": use native nesting (",[18,1401,214],{},") for component-scoped styles — ",[18,1404,1405],{},".card { & .title { ... } &:hover { ... } }"," is Sass-like nesting, native in 2023+. Reduces repetition and keeps related styles together. Use ",[18,1408,214],{}," for compound selectors (",[18,1411,249],{},[18,1413,253],{},[225,1415,1416,1375,1418,1420,1421,1424],{},[1372,1417,1374],{},[18,1419,1016],{}," to derive shades\u002Ftints from a base color — ",[18,1422,1423],{},"color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 80%, white)"," gives a lighter shade, no preprocessor. Useful for hover\u002Factive states from a single token.",[225,1426,1427,1375,1429,1431,1432,1434,1435,1437,1438,1441,1442,1444],{},[1372,1428,1374],{},[18,1430,1044],{}," for headings and ",[18,1433,1048],{}," for paragraphs — ",[18,1436,1073],{}," evens heading line lengths (no manual ",[18,1439,1440],{},"\u003Cbr>","), ",[18,1443,1048],{}," avoids a single word on the last paragraph line. Free typography polish, no JS.",[23,1446,1448],{"id":1447},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[222,1450,1451,1465,1476,1499,1508,1528,1558,1575,1589,1598],{},[225,1452,1453,1458,1459,1461,1462,1464],{},[1372,1454,1455,1457],{},[18,1456,20],{}," is not a performance problem anymore",": early concerns about ",[18,1460,20],{}," performance have been addressed in modern browsers. But very deep ",[18,1463,20],{}," (checking many descendants) can still be slower than a simple class — use judiciously.",[225,1466,1467,61,1472,1475],{},[1372,1468,1469,1471],{},[18,1470,20],{}," can't be nested inside itself in all engines",[18,1473,1474],{},":has(:has(...))"," has limited support. Avoid deep nesting.",[225,1477,1478,61,1485,1488,1489,1492,1493,1495,1496,1498],{},[1372,1479,1480,1481,1484],{},"Cascade layer order is set by the ",[353,1482,1483],{},"first"," declaration",[18,1486,1487],{},"@layer reset, base;"," sets the order. Later ",[18,1490,1491],{},"@layer base { ... }"," adds to the existing ",[18,1494,758],{}," layer, in its position. If you ",[18,1497,560],{}," without a prior order declaration, the order is by first appearance.",[225,1500,1501,1504,1505,1507],{},[1372,1502,1503],{},"Unlayered styles beat layered styles",": a rule outside any ",[18,1506,560],{}," wins over all layered rules (regardless of specificity). This is why you might put utilities in a layer (to be beatable by unlayered overrides) or keep your custom CSS unlayered.",[225,1509,1510,61,1514,236,1516,1518,1519,236,1521,1524,1525,1527],{},[1372,1511,260,1512,536],{},[18,1513,214],{},[18,1515,239],{},[18,1517,273],{}," (0,2,0). ",[18,1520,253],{},[18,1522,1523],{},".card.active"," (0,2,0). The ",[18,1526,214],{}," is substituted, so the specificity is the combined selector's.",[225,1529,1530,61,1536,1538,1539,1541,1542,1544,1545,1547,1548,1550,1551,250,1553,1555,1556,240],{},[1372,1531,1532,1533,1535],{},"Nesting without ",[18,1534,214],{}," is a descendant",[18,1537,235],{}," inside ",[18,1540,47],{}," (no ",[18,1543,214],{},") = ",[18,1546,273],{},". Use ",[18,1549,214],{}," for compound (",[18,1552,249],{},[18,1554,253],{},") and when you need the parent at a non-start position (",[18,1557,256],{},[225,1559,1560,61,1565,1568,1569,1571,1572,1574],{},[1372,1561,1562,1563],{},"Container style queries check ",[353,1564,932],{},[18,1566,1567],{},"@container style(--theme: dark)"," checks the container's ",[18,1570,936],{}," variable. You can't query standard properties (like ",[18,1573,814],{},") in a style query — only custom properties.",[225,1576,1577,1582,1583,1585,1586,1588],{},[1372,1578,1579,1581],{},[18,1580,1044],{}," on long text",": it's for short text (headings). On long paragraphs, ",[18,1584,1073],{}," can look worse (uneven). Use ",[18,1587,1048],{}," for paragraphs.",[225,1590,1591,61,1594,1597],{},[1372,1592,1593],{},"View transitions need a DOM update",[18,1595,1596],{},"document.startViewTransition(() => { \u002F* update DOM *\u002F })"," — the callback updates the DOM, and the API animates between the old and new states. The old state is captured before the callback.",[225,1599,1600,61,1603,1606],{},[1372,1601,1602],{},"Scroll-driven animations are newer",[18,1604,1605],{},"animation-timeline: scroll()"," is Chrome 115+\u002FSafari 17.4+. Provide a JS fallback for older browsers (or accept no animation).",[23,1608,1610],{"id":1609},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1612,1613,1614,1616],{},"A developer uses ",[18,1615,20],{}," to style a form section with an error, but it's not working:",[28,1618,1619],{"language":30},[32,1620,1622],{"className":34,"code":1621,"language":30,"meta":36,"style":36},".form-section:has(.error) {\n    border-color: red;\n}\n.form-section {\n    border: 2px solid #ccc;\n}\n",[18,1623,1624,1634,1645,1649,1656,1675],{"__ignoreMap":36},[40,1625,1626,1628,1630,1632],{"class":42,"line":43},[40,1627,405],{"class":46},[40,1629,327],{"class":50},[40,1631,410],{"class":46},[40,1633,178],{"class":50},[40,1635,1636,1639,1641,1643],{"class":42,"line":54},[40,1637,1638],{"class":57},"    border-color",[40,1640,61],{"class":50},[40,1642,420],{"class":57},[40,1644,71],{"class":50},[40,1646,1647],{"class":42,"line":74},[40,1648,208],{"class":50},[40,1650,1651,1654],{"class":42,"line":81},[40,1652,1653],{"class":46},".form-section",[40,1655,51],{"class":50},[40,1657,1658,1661,1663,1665,1667,1670,1673],{"class":42,"line":106},[40,1659,1660],{"class":57},"    border",[40,1662,61],{"class":50},[40,1664,192],{"class":57},[40,1666,175],{"class":67},[40,1668,1669],{"class":57}," solid",[40,1671,1672],{"class":57}," #ccc",[40,1674,71],{"class":50},[40,1676,1677],{"class":42,"line":127},[40,1678,208],{"class":50},[14,1680,1681],{},"What's wrong?",[1683,1684,1685,1689,1715,1762,1782,1818,1842,1845,1894,1903],"details",{},[1686,1687,1688],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1690,1691,1692,1695,1696,1698,1699,1701,1702,1704,1705,1707,1708,1710,1711,1714],{},"Specificity and source order. ",[18,1693,1694],{},".form-section:has(.error)"," has specificity (0,2,0) — ",[18,1697,1653],{}," (0,1,0) + ",[18,1700,410],{}," (0,1,0) inside ",[18,1703,20],{},". ",[18,1706,1653],{}," alone is (0,1,0). So the ",[18,1709,20],{}," rule has ",[353,1712,1713],{},"higher"," specificity and should win...",[14,1716,1717,1718,61,1721,1723,1724,1727,1728,1730,1731,1733,1734,1737,1738,1740,1741,1744,1745,1748,1749,1751,1752,1754,1755,1757,1758,1761],{},"The actual bug is ",[1372,1719,1720],{},"source order",[18,1722,1694],{}," comes ",[353,1725,1726],{},"before"," ",[18,1729,1653],{},". Both set ",[18,1732,415],{}," (well, the second sets ",[18,1735,1736],{},"border",", which is a shorthand that includes ",[18,1739,415],{},"). ",[18,1742,1743],{},".form-section { border: 2px solid #ccc; }"," sets ",[18,1746,1747],{},"border-color: #ccc"," (via the shorthand). Since ",[18,1750,1694],{}," is (0,2,0) and ",[18,1753,1653],{}," is (0,1,0), the ",[18,1756,20],{}," rule wins — so ",[18,1759,1760],{},"border-color: red"," should apply...",[14,1763,1764,1765,1767,1768,1771,1772,1774,1775,1778,1779,1781],{},"Hmm, actually the ",[18,1766,20],{}," rule ",[353,1769,1770],{},"should"," work. Let me reconsider. The issue might be that ",[18,1773,410],{}," is not a ",[353,1776,1777],{},"direct"," child but a deeper descendant — ",[18,1780,20],{}," checks all descendants, so that's fine.",[14,1783,1784,1785,1805,1806,1808,1809,1811,1812,1814,1815,1817],{},"The real bug: ",[1372,1786,1787,1788,1723,1790,1793,1794,1796,1797,1799,1800,1727,1803],{},"the second rule ",[18,1789,1743],{},[353,1791,1792],{},"after"," the ",[18,1795,20],{}," rule, and the ",[18,1798,1736],{}," shorthand ",[353,1801,1802],{},"resets",[18,1804,415],{},". Even though ",[18,1807,1694],{}," has higher specificity (0,2,0 > 0,1,0), the shorthand ",[18,1810,1736],{}," in the second rule sets ",[18,1813,1747],{}," with specificity (0,1,0). Specificity wins over source order, so the ",[18,1816,20],{}," rule (0,2,0) should still win...",[14,1819,1820,1821,1767,1823,1826,1827,1832,1833,1841],{},"Actually, the ",[18,1822,20],{},[353,1824,1825],{},"does"," win by specificity. So if it's \"not working,\" the likely cause is ",[1372,1828,1829,1831],{},[18,1830,20],{}," browser support"," (older browsers) or ",[1372,1834,1835,1836,1838,1839],{},"the ",[18,1837,410],{}," element isn't a descendant of ",[18,1840,1653],{}," (maybe a sibling or in a different container).",[14,1843,1844],{},"The most pragmatic fix — ensure source order and specificity are clear:",[32,1846,1848],{"className":34,"code":1847,"language":30,"meta":36,"style":36},".form-section { border: 2px solid #ccc; }  \u002F* base, first *\u002F\n.form-section:has(.error) { border-color: red; }  \u002F* override, after *\u002F\n",[18,1849,1850,1873],{"__ignoreMap":36},[40,1851,1852,1854,1856,1858,1860,1862,1864,1866,1868,1870],{"class":42,"line":43},[40,1853,1653],{"class":46},[40,1855,90],{"class":50},[40,1857,1736],{"class":57},[40,1859,61],{"class":50},[40,1861,192],{"class":57},[40,1863,175],{"class":67},[40,1865,1669],{"class":57},[40,1867,1672],{"class":57},[40,1869,860],{"class":50},[40,1871,1872],{"class":300},"\u002F* base, first *\u002F\n",[40,1874,1875,1877,1879,1881,1883,1885,1887,1889,1891],{"class":42,"line":54},[40,1876,405],{"class":46},[40,1878,327],{"class":50},[40,1880,410],{"class":46},[40,1882,381],{"class":50},[40,1884,415],{"class":57},[40,1886,61],{"class":50},[40,1888,420],{"class":57},[40,1890,860],{"class":50},[40,1892,1893],{"class":300},"\u002F* override, after *\u002F\n",[14,1895,1896,1897,1899,1900,1902],{},"::\nAnd verify in a ",[18,1898,20],{},"-supporting browser (Chrome 105+, Safari 15.4+, Firefox 121+) that ",[18,1901,410],{}," is a descendant.",[14,1904,1905,1908,1909,1911,1912,1767,1914,1916],{},[1372,1906,1907],{},"The lesson",": when ",[18,1910,20],{}," \"doesn't work,\" check (1) browser support, (2) that the matched element is actually a descendant, (3) source order — put the ",[18,1913,20],{},[353,1915,1792],{}," the base rule. Specificity (0,2,0 > 0,1,0) should win, but source order is a clearer intent.",[23,1918,1919],{"id":1686},"Summary",[14,1921,1922,1923,1441,1925,1927,1928,1930,1931,1441,1934,250,1936,250,1938,1142,1940,1942],{},"You can now use native nesting (",[18,1924,214],{},[18,1926,20],{}," (the parent selector), cascade layers (",[18,1929,560],{},"), container style queries (",[18,1932,1933],{},"@container style(--var: ...)",[18,1935,943],{},[18,1937,1016],{},[18,1939,1044],{},[18,1941,1048],{},", scroll-driven animations, and view transitions — the modern CSS features that replace JS and preprocessor workarounds. Next: architecture and methodology.",[1944,1945,1946],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .sk71V, html code.shiki .sk71V{--shiki-default:#22863A;--shiki-github-dark:#85E89D}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text